7. Cluster Metrics and Monitoring
OpenShift uses Prometheus for monitoring.
Prometheus collects metrics from services.
Metrics endpoint:
/metrics
Applications expose performance data through this endpoint.
Example metrics:
•	CPU usage
•	memory usage
•	request rate
•	error rate
________________________________________
8. ServiceMonitor and PodMonitor
To monitor services and pods, OpenShift uses monitoring resources.
ServiceMonitor
Defines how a service is monitored.
Example tasks:
•	collect metrics
•	define monitoring rules
________________________________________
PodMonitor
Monitors individual pods.
Used when metrics come directly from pods.
________________________________________
9. Alerts
Alerts notify administrators when something goes wrong.
Example alerts:
•	pod crash
•	high CPU usage
•	node failure
•	service unavailable
Alert workflow:
Metric collected
       ↓
Monitor checks threshold
       ↓
Condition fails
       ↓
Alert triggered
Example:
Web server port 80 not responding
Alert severity types:
•	warning
•	critical
________________________________________
10. Metrics Dashboard (Observe Panel)
Menu:
Observe → Metrics
This page uses Grafana-like visualization.
Administrators can:
•	query metrics
•	create graphs
•	build dashboards
Example metrics queries:
CPU usage
Memory usage
Pod network traffic
CLI example:
oc adm top nodes
or
oc adm top pods
________________________________________
11. Alerting Dashboard
Menu:
Observe → Alerting
This page shows:
•	active alerts
•	alert severity
•	alert description
•	affected components
Administrators use this to identify system failures quickly.
________________________________________
12. Kubernetes Events
Events show important cluster activities.
They are a high-level summary of logs.
Examples:
•	pod created
•	pod failed
•	node restarted
•	deployment scaled
Menu:
Home → Events
CLI equivalent:
oc get events
Events help administrators quickly understand what changed in the cluster.
________________________________________
Logs vs Events
Feature	Logs	Events
Detail level	Very detailed	High-level
Purpose	debugging	monitoring
Scope	application/system	cluster activity
________________________________________
